The variance of the sample is $\text{Var}(\bar{X}) = \frac{\sigma^2}{n} = \frac{\mu^2}{n} = \frac{3^2}{36} = \frac{9}{36} = \frac{1}{4}$.
The standard deviation of the sample is $\sigma_{\bar{X}} = \sqrt{\text{Var}(\bar{X})} = \sqrt{\frac{1}{4}} = \frac{1}{2} = 0.5$.
